# Copy to dev/.env.local (git-ignored) and fill in. The API's `npm run start` reads dev/.env.local on its own.
# Never commit dev/.env.local, and never reuse these values anywhere real.
#
#   cp dev/.env.example dev/.env.local
#
# 32 random bytes, base64. Encrypts room secrets in the database. Make one with:  openssl rand -base64 32
# COLOC_SECRETS_KEY=<paste the output here, or let docs/dev.md append it for you>

# Lets you log in as anyone from the seeded city. Development only: the API ignores it when COLOC_PUBLIC_URL is https,
# and `npm run up` turns it off while it shares the city.
COLOC_DEV_LOGIN=1

# `npm run up` adds this laptop's own database password, database URL and caretaker key below on its first run
# (COLOC_DB_PASSWORD, COLOC_DATABASE_URL, COLOC_DEV_AGENT_SECRET). Keep them; never commit them.

# The "Reset the demo city" button in the lobby's settings, for the logins in COLOC_ADMINS (comma list).
# With the dev login on and no list, the admins are the seeded "jib" and "Djbrl". The dev login is always off on a
# site served over https, so on a shared city only the GitHub logins listed here are admins.
COLOC_DEMO_RESET=1
# COLOC_ADMINS=Djbrl,your-github-login

# Where the tutorial's sample app comes from. GitHub can't be reached without credentials while the repo is
# private, so point it at your own clone on disk. It must be an absolute file:// path to a clone with `main` checked in,
# and the workshop's caretaker may build only that clone (`npm run up` passes it as COLOC_ALLOW_LOCAL_REPOS; docs/dev.md, step 6).
# COLOC_TUTORIAL_REPO=file:///absolute/path/to/la-coloc
# COLOC_TUTORIAL_PATH=examples/hello

# The address you open the site at. GitHub login comes back here, and only pages from this origin may open the
# lobby's live line. The default is the dev site's: http://localhost:5175
# COLOC_PUBLIC_URL=http://localhost:5175
